{%- comment -%}
  Section: siwa-oracle-invite | Owner: A-06 | Task: ST-07

  USF-01, Section 7 — the Oracle's dedicated homepage home. Phlur's slot 4 is
  a 608px full-bleed programme banner; the bible fills it with the quiz
  explainer, and the load-bearing half of its brief is "with visual
  explanation of the flow". A banner with a heading and a button is not an
  explanation, so the flow is actually drawn: C-02 FeatureRow puts the image
  on one side and, on the other, a numbered ladder of the questions the
  Oracle asks before it speaks.

  THIS SECTION IS NOT THE QUIZ.
  D-01 OracleQuiz / QuizStep / QuizProgress / QuizResult are a separate P0
  feature with their own components and their own behaviour. This surface
  invites into it and sets the expectation; the CTA points wherever the
  merchant put the quiz. Nothing here holds state, so nothing here needs a
  line of JavaScript — and section-level JavaScript is a CI error in this
  theme regardless (the behaviour layer is assets/siwa-theme.js).

  THE SIX STEPS ARE BLOCKS, NOT A RANGE LOOP.
  `{% for i in (1..6) %}` would give the merchant six rows they cannot edit,
  reorder or delete, and the bible's failure list opens with "generic
  questions that could apply to any product category" — which is exactly what
  uneditable placeholder rows become. They are `section.blocks` of type
  `step`, drag-reorderable in the Customizer, each carrying
  `{{ block.shopify_attributes }}` so the theme editor can select one.

  They render as an <ol> because they are a sequence: a screen reader should
  announce "list, 6 items" and count through them, which a stack of <div>s
  never does. The visible number comes from `sections.oracle.step`
  interpolated with `forloop.index` — there is no digit typed into this file,
  and the word "Step" is the locale's, so Arabic reads "خطوة ١" and not a
  Latin label with an Arabic sentence after it.

  NOTHING HERE IS TYPED COPY.
  · eyebrow / heading / body / CTA label are schema settings that fall back to
    `sections.oracle.*` when the merchant leaves them blank — the store ships
    saying something true in both languages before anyone opens the editor.
  · The Oracle's name is `general.brand.oracle_name`, never a literal. It is
    the most-repeated proper noun in the store and the Arabic naming decision
    is still open (الحكيم today), so one edit to the dictionary has to be able
    to rename it everywhere. It is read twice here: as the accessible name of
    the region, and as the sigil that stands in for an unset image.
  · Every step's label and text are block settings.

  ONE GOLD PER FOLD (principle 1).
  This fold spends its gold on the Oracle's CTA and nowhere else: the step
  spine, the markers and the numbers are drawn in --colors-border-strong and
  --colors-text-secondary, not in gold, so the single gold object on the band
  is the thing the bible wants clicked. `cta_variant` still exposes secondary
  and tester, because a merchant who also runs the hero's gold CTA inside
  this same viewport needs a way to step this one down.

  MOBILE IS THE PRIMARY CASE, NOT THE FALLBACK.
  70%+ of Siwa's traffic is mobile and the bible calls a quiz that is not
  mobile-optimised a failure outright. .siwa-feature-row collapses to one
  column at 768px on its own; the step ladder stacks its number above its
  copy rather than beside it below that breakpoint, the media well swaps to a
  landscape ratio so it cannot eat the first screen, and the CTA goes
  full-width at 480px. See assets/siwa-oracle-invite.css.

  GATE 0 FINDING F2.
  Anything a media query has to override later is emitted INSIDE a matching
  media query. The desktop padding pair is set on the bare scoped selector;
  the mobile pair is set again inside `@media (max-width: 768px)`. Emitting
  the mobile values at section scope would out-rank every class-level query
  in the stylesheet and freeze one value at all widths — the trap
  siwa-footer.liquid documents on its column count.
{%- endcomment -%}

{{ 'siwa-oracle-invite.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings

  comment
    Setting blank → locale key. The house pattern: a merchant's words win, and
    the translated line is what ships until they type any.
  endcomment
  assign eyebrow = s.eyebrow
  if eyebrow == blank
    assign eyebrow = 'sections.oracle.eyebrow' | t
  endif

  assign heading = s.heading
  if heading == blank
    assign heading = 'sections.oracle.heading' | t
  endif

  comment
    `body` is richtext; if the schema field is blank the locale value is used.
    The fallback is wrapped in paragraph tags so it renders inside .siwa-prose.
  endcomment
  assign body_html = s.body
  if body_html == blank
    assign body_html = 'sections.oracle.body' | t | prepend: '<p>' | append: '</p>'
  endif

  assign cta_label = s.cta_label
  if cta_label == blank
    assign cta_label = 'sections.oracle.cta' | t
  endif

  assign oracle_name = 'general.brand.oracle_name' | t
  assign image_alt = s.image_alt | escape
  assign heading_id = 'siwa-oracle-heading-' | append: section.id

  comment
    Which side the media sits on is `order` under the hood — one of the two
    documented physical exceptions (DESIGN.md §5), already mirrored inside
    .siwa-feature-row--reverse. Nothing to mirror here.
  endcomment
  assign row_class = 'siwa-feature-row siwa-oracle-invite__row'
  if s.media_position == 'inline-end'
    assign row_class = row_class | append: ' siwa-feature-row--reverse'
  endif

  comment
    The dark scheme inverts through the design system's `.on-dark` band, which
    re-points the semantic tokens per preset (assets/siwa-themes.css). This
    section invents no palette of its own.
  endcomment
  assign band_class = 'siwa-oracle-invite siwa-oracle-invite--' | append: s.color_scheme
  assign band_class = band_class | append: ' siwa-oracle-invite--rhythm-' | append: s.rhythm
  if s.color_scheme == 'dark'
    assign band_class = band_class | append: ' on-dark'
  endif
-%}

{% style %}
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .siwa-oracle-invite__inner {
    --siwa-oracle-pad-start: {{ s.padding_top }}px;
    --siwa-oracle-pad-end: {{ s.padding_bottom }}px;
  }

  {%- comment -%}
    F2. Inside the query, not at section scope — see the header comment.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .siwa-oracle-invite__inner {
      --siwa-oracle-pad-start: {{ s.mobile_padding_top }}px;
      --siwa-oracle-pad-end: {{ s.mobile_padding_bottom }}px;
    }
  }
{% endstyle %}

<section class="{{ band_class }}" aria-label="{{ oracle_name | escape }}">
  <div class="siwa-container siwa-oracle-invite__inner">
    <div class="{{ row_class }}">
      <div class="siwa-feature-row__media siwa-media siwa-oracle-invite__media">
        {%- if s.image != blank -%}
          {{
            s.image
            | image_url: width: 1400
            | image_tag:
              class: 'siwa-oracle-invite__image',
              alt: image_alt,
              loading: 'lazy',
              widths: '400, 600, 800, 1000, 1200, 1400',
              sizes: '(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 50vw'
          }}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            No image yet: a sigil rather than a grey placeholder box. The name
            is the locale key, so this stands in correctly in both languages.
            aria-hidden because the eyebrow and the region name already carry
            it — a screen reader should hear it once, not three times.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <p class="siwa-oracle-invite__sigil" aria-hidden="true">{{ oracle_name }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      <div class="siwa-feature-row__body siwa-oracle-invite__body">
        <p class="siwa-label siwa-oracle-invite__eyebrow">{{ eyebrow }}</p>
        <h2 class="siwa-h2 siwa-oracle-invite__heading" id="{{ heading_id }}">{{ heading }}</h2>
        <div class="siwa-prose siwa-oracle-invite__text">{{ body_html }}</div>

        {%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
          <ol class="siwa-oracle-invite__steps" aria-labelledby="{{ heading_id }}">
            {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
              <li class="siwa-oracle-invite__step" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                <span class="siwa-label siwa-oracle-invite__step-number">
                  {{- 'sections.oracle.step' | t: number: forloop.index -}}
                </span>
                {%- if block.settings.label != blank -%}
                  <span class="siwa-oracle-invite__step-label">{{ block.settings.label }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- if block.settings.text != blank -%}
                  <span class="siwa-oracle-invite__step-text">{{ block.settings.text }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
              </li>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ol>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          No link, no control. A CTA that goes nowhere is a dead control, and
          an invitation with a button that does not open the quiz is worse
          than an invitation with none.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if s.cta_url != blank -%}
          <div class="siwa-cluster siwa-oracle-invite__cta">
            {%- render 'siwa-button', label: cta_label, href: s.cta_url, variant: s.cta_variant -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Oracle invitation",
  "tag": "div",
  "class": "siwa-oracle-invite-section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Content"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "sections.oracle.schema_intro"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow",
      "info": "Blank uses the translated eyebrow."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "info": "Blank uses the translated heading. Say what happens, not what it is — \"Six questions. Then the Oracle speaks.\", never \"Find your scent\"."
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "body",
      "label": "Body",
      "info": "Blank uses the translated line, which already names the tester. Whatever you write, keep the tester in it — a reading nobody can try is a guess."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "cta_label",
      "label": "Button label",
      "info": "Blank uses the translated label. Name the act, not the mechanism — \"Ask the Oracle\", never \"Learn more\" (DESIGN.md §8, anti-pattern 11)."
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "cta_url",
      "label": "Button link",
      "info": "Point it at the quiz. With no link the invitation renders without its button rather than shipping a control that goes nowhere."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "cta_variant",
      "label": "Button treatment",
      "info": "Gold is rationed one to a fold (principle 1). This fold is where it belongs — unless the hero's gold CTA is still on screen beside it, in which case step this one down.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "primary", "label": "Gold — the strongest action on the band" },
        { "value": "secondary", "label": "Outline" },
        { "value": "tester", "label": "Tester outline" }
      ],
      "default": "primary"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Media"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image",
      "label": "Image",
      "info": "Real product or workshop photography (DESIGN.md §8, anti-pattern 15). With no image the Oracle's name stands in its place."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "image_alt",
      "label": "Image description",
      "info": "What a reader who cannot see it would need to know. Leave blank if the image only decorates — the picture then announces nothing rather than announcing noise."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "media_position",
      "label": "Image side",
      "info": "Mirrors automatically in Arabic. Below 768px the image always sits above the explanation.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "inline-start", "label": "Start of the line" },
        { "value": "inline-end", "label": "End of the line" }
      ],
      "default": "inline-start"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Layout & spacing"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "rhythm",
      "label": "Vertical rhythm",
      "info": "Ceremonial is the section rhythm; dense is the commerce one. DESIGN.md §4 asks that the two alternate down the page.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "section", "label": "Ceremonial — full section rhythm" },
        { "value": "tight", "label": "Dense — commerce rhythm" }
      ],
      "default": "section"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "label": "Extra padding top",
      "info": "Added on top of the rhythm above, so the rhythm keeps working when this is 0.",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 96,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "label": "Extra padding bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 96,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "mobile_padding_top",
      "label": "Extra padding top (mobile)",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 96,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "mobile_padding_bottom",
      "label": "Extra padding bottom (mobile)",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 96,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "Ground",
      "info": "Ink inverts the band through the design system's .on-dark tokens, which every design direction supplies its own values for. No colour is set here.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "page", "label": "Page — the parchment ground" },
        { "value": "surface", "label": "Sand — one step up from the page" },
        { "value": "dark", "label": "Ink — inverted band" }
      ],
      "default": "surface"
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "step",
      "name": "Step",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "One question the Oracle asks. The number in front of it is counted and translated for you — do not type it. Ask something only a fragrance house could ask: \"What's your style?\" is the failure the feature bible names by name."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "label",
          "label": "Step label",
          "info": "Three to five words."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "text",
          "label": "Step text",
          "info": "One concrete sentence. Sensory before technical (DESIGN.md §7.1)."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 6,
  "default": {
    "blocks": [
      { "type": "step", "settings": { "label": "", "text": "" } },
      { "type": "step", "settings": { "label": "", "text": "" } },
      { "type": "step", "settings": { "label": "", "text": "" } },
      { "type": "step", "settings": { "label": "", "text": "" } },
      { "type": "step", "settings": { "label": "", "text": "" } },
      { "type": "step", "settings": { "label": "", "text": "" } }
    ]
  },
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Oracle invitation",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "step", "settings": { "label": "", "text": "" } },
        { "type": "step", "settings": { "label": "", "text": "" } },
        { "type": "step", "settings": { "label": "", "text": "" } },
        { "type": "step", "settings": { "label": "", "text": "" } },
        { "type": "step", "settings": { "label": "", "text": "" } },
        { "type": "step", "settings": { "label": "", "text": "" } }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
